SUSPECTED BUG: Durability returns fmt.Errorf("source: flush %s: %w", f.Name(),
flush(f)); in the default build flush only returns nil. fmt.Errorf never returns nil, so
the function ALWAYS returns a non-nil error with nothing to unwrap (main prints
"source: flush /dev/stdout: %!w(<nil>)"). Expected: 1 entry, opaque fmt.Errorf "source:
flush %s: %w", which is what the tool prints for a literal nil or a nil local variable
as %w operand. Actual: "0 entries", i.e. the tool claims the function cannot return an
error. Same cause as save_join_nil_operand: the empty value set of the call operand
erases the Wrap when the callee summary is substituted.
-- args --
source/source.go:@durability
